 "standard_url": "https://www.education.gov.za/Portals/0/CD/National%20Curriculum%20Statements%20and%20Vocational/CAPS%20SP%20%20MATHEMATICS%20GR%207-9.pdf",
 "standard_text": "Use commutative, associative and distributive laws for rational numbers and laws of exponents to multiply integers, monomials and binomials by polynomials, divide polynomials by integers or monomials, determine the product of two binomials, and determine the square of a binomial; simplify algebraic expressions involving the above operations.",
 "meta_desc": "Free CAPS Grade 9 algebraic expressions worksheets: simplifying, expanding, products of binomials, squares of binomials and algebraic fractions. 100 questions with memos.",
 "key_big": "(a + b)² = a² + 2ab + b².",
 "key_sub": "Multiply every term by every term.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Expand: multiply every term in one bracket by every term in the other.</li><li>(x + 3)(x − 5) = x² − 5x + 3x − 15 = x² − 2x − 15.</li><li>(a + b)² = a² + 2ab + b². Do not forget the middle term.</li><li>Simplify algebraic fractions by cancelling common factors.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>(2x − 3)²</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>(2x)² − 2 × 2x × 3 + 3²</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 4x² − 12x + 9</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>(a + b)² = a² + b²</td><td>Add the middle term 2ab.</td></tr><tr><td>Some terms only</td><td>Multiply every term.</td></tr><tr><td>Signs</td><td>(−3) × (−5) = +15.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
